    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (81.94) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Elmer Rodr\u00edguez, whose elevated xERA of 5.31 provides the high-leverage environment needed for our top-tier assets to produce multi-category contributions. **Kyle Tucker** gains an additional boost from wind conditions blowing out, and despite the slight park penalty, his elite floor makes him the day\u2019s must-start centerpiece. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from similar SP weakness and an optimal #3 spot in the order, cementing his role as our primary source for power and run production.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes efficiency over raw volume, which necessitated the difficult benching of **Liam Hicks** (39.22). Despite a favorable platoon advantage against Wheeler, the elite 3.16 xERA of his opposing pitcher dragged his efficiency score just below our 40.0 threshold, opting for the safer projection of **Coby Mayo** (54.85). We are monitoring the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.08) and **Heliot Ramos** (58.18); while both are currently projected for strong days, their pending lineup status introduces volatility. Specifically, **Heliot Ramos** sits on the cusp of our marginal tier, though his projected #3 slot against Baz should provide sufficient volume to justify the start. \n\nThe strategy remains focused on maximizing category output while mitigating the risk of game-cap depletion. **Nasim Nunez** (47.12) is active primarily for his speed potential; while his #9 order position limits his upside, his agility remains a requisite tool in our 5x5 build. Conversely, **Sam Antonacci** (48.78) faces a challenging platoon disadvantage against Freeland, which suppressed his score. We will continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and the injured **Luis Robert Jr.** in reserve while maintaining depth with **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Drake Baldwin** to ensure the Austin Waves remain competitive through the final weekend of the campaign.",
